Under authority contained in the act of Congress approved June 25, 1910
(36 Stat., 847), as amended by the act of August 24, 1912 (37 Stat., 497), and
subject to all provisions, limitations, exceptions and conditions of said acts, it
is hereby ordered that the following described tract of land on Kodiak Island,
Alaska, be, and the same is hereby temporarily withdrawn from settlement,
location, sale or entry and reserved for use of the Department of Agriculture as
an addition to the U. S. Agricultural Experiment Station situated near Kodiak,
Kodiak Island, Alaska, created by Executive Order dated March 28, 1898, viz:
beginning at a point N.. 340 43' W., 2.55 chs. distant from the true point
for meander corner No. 3 of amended U. S. Survey No. 1272, U. S. Agricultural
Experiment Station, and on line between corners Nos. 3 and 4 of said survey,
which point is corner No. i of U. S. Survey No. 1389, Addition to U. S. Agri-
cultural Experiment Station ;
